 "nodes": [
  {
   "id": "n3",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**1. What it is** ✓\nWhy is it held?\nUSE → PPE · EARN (rent/value) → Investment property · SELL → Inventory\nTAS 40 = land & buildings only; rented-out cars = PPE\n⚠ shaky: put a rented-out building and rental cars in the wrong bucket (2 ghost cards). Car dealer split = right.\n10 Nov 🟩: both sorting cards passed cold (box 2) + TAS 40 ghost ✓ 7 Nov",
   "x": 880,
   "y": -80,
   "width": 400,
   "height": 250,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "n4",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**2. Recognition** ✓\n① PROBABLE future benefits flow to the entity\n② cost MEASURED RELIABLY\n(never 'certain')\nsolid: built both conditions himself",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 180,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "n13",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**4. Subsequent costs**\nrepairs → expense\nreplacement / major inspection → asset · s44\n26 Oct (GPT): covered · recheck: old component's CA is derecognised (not netted against the new cost) · major inspection = capitalise, routine cleaning = expense",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 1620,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n15",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Revaluation\nwhole class · method (a) proportional / (b) eliminate AD\n⚠ s54 + s57 have errors\n26 Oct: both methods ✓ (elimination step 2 slipped 50k→30k; skipped ratio/running balances on proportional). Surplus = FV − CA either way\n7 Nov: 2021 final P2(a) ⚠ elimination entries + used 3 years for 2 → re-taught (2-step table) → fresh equipment problem ✓.",
   "x": 1380,
   "y": 1800,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n16",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Up / down\nincrease → OCI surplus · decrease → P&L loss · reversals cross over · s61–65\n⚠ 26 Oct: first up → said 'gain' (it's OCI surplus) · cross-over excess → said OCI (it's P&L) · reversal of a P&L loss ✓\n⚠ 3 Nov: cross-over decrease → said ALL to P&L (surplus 30k first, only 10k excess to P&L), carded · elimination step 2 down ✓ (10k loss) but wrote 'land' twice (carded) · 3 Nov: up-side reversal → sent all 40k to surplus (25k P&L gain first), carded · down-side retry ✓ (15k/15k)\n10 Nov 🟧: cross-over cards 36 + 37 still unpassed; 6 Nov reval-up clearing entry ✗",
   "x": 1380,
   "y": 1980,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n17",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Surplus → retained earnings\nnot through P&L · s66–67\n⚠ 26 Oct: said surplus is 'recognised on sale' TWICE → fixed: excess-dep transfer 10k/yr + sale → Dr surplus / Cr RE ✓\n⏸ 3 Nov 10:40 PAUSED HERE (MK work): next cold Q = surplus 60,000, 6 yrs remaining → yearly transfer 10,000 Dr Surplus / Cr RE (excess dep). Revaluation up/down/history chain ✓ 3 Nov (3-year sequence clean). Then → Impairment (deck read, first Q ready: CA 500k, FVLCTS 420k, VIU 450k → RA 450k, loss 50k)\n3 Nov 17:33 ✓ CLOSED: yearly transfer 10k ✓ · sale → remaining 40k Dr surplus / Cr RE ✓ (asked if it 'goes away': no, straight to RE, never P&L)\n7 Nov: ⚠ AGAIN ×2 (card 40: 'share capital inside P&L' · card 48: surplus on sale → P&L). Then equipment chain (b) transfer 20k → RE ✓.\n10 Nov: ⚠ excess-dep transfer needed re-teaching (card 40 ✗; 'bucket + scoop' landed, 20k ✓) · reval → sale chain: gain 1M to P&L ✓, surplus → RE ✓, BOTH entries clean ✓\n🟧 10 Nov: missed 7 Nov ×2 and needed the re-teach today. The sale step is clean; the yearly transfer isn't automatic yet",
   "x": 1380,
   "y": 2160,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 248,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n14",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**5. After recognition**\ncost model vs revaluation model · s46–67\n26 Oct: done in the Room, all sub-branches drilled",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 1980,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n19",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Methods\nstraight-line · sum-of-years' digits · declining balance · units · hours\n⚠ 26 Oct: straight-line ✓ · SYD forgotten → example → ✓ (150k/120k) · double-declining forgotten → used the example's rate + took residual out first → fixed ✓ (rate 2/n, on CA, residual = floor) · units: method ✓, rounded 0.222 → 99,900 (go per unit: ฿5 × 20k = 100k)\n10 Nov 🟩: SYD + DDB cards (3) all passed cold",
   "x": 1380,
   "y": 2428,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "n20",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Start / stop · reviews ← next\nchange = change in ESTIMATE\n26 Oct: depreciation starts when READY for use ✓ (warehouse Q). PAUSED here 13:22: next cold Q = change in estimate (500k, residual 50k, SL 5 yrs, after 2 yrs life revised to 4 MORE years → yr 3 = (320k − 50k) ÷ 4 = 67,500, prospective)\n29 Oct ✓ CLOSED: change in estimate 67,500 w/ working · prospective vs error retrospective ✓ · idle keeps depreciating ✓ · ⚠ stops at EARLIER of held-for-sale (TFRS 5) / derecognised: missed held-for-sale (carded)\n10 Nov 🟧: cards 'restate yrs 1–2?' + 'two events that stop depreciation' unpassed",
   "x": 1380,
   "y": 2598,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n21",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Depletion\nnatural resources, per unit · s93–95\n29 Oct: ⚠ missed per-unit rate (said 300k → 1,500,000) + revised rate used ORIGINAL cost (10 → 6.25); both fixed on retry, carded\n10 Nov 🟩: both depletion cards passed cold",
   "x": 1380,
   "y": 2788,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "n18",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**6. Depreciation** ✓ CLOSED 29 Oct\ncomponents · depreciable amount = cost − residual · s69–91\n29 Oct: components ✓ (plane 5,333,333)\n29 Oct: ⚠ DDB yr 2 missed (112,500 vs 120,000), fixed on a fresh Q + floor ✓ (20,000) · SYD ✓ (n(n+1)/2, × cost − residual) · open: does the lecturer teach the DDB→SL switch? check summary mid2",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 2520,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "n22",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**7. Derecognition** ✓ 29 Oct\ngain/loss = proceeds − carrying amount\nnever revenue · s99–100\n29 Oct: sale mid-year ✓ (half-yr dep, CA 275,000, gain 5,000) · ⚠ P&L not revenue ✓ but wobbled to OCI (carded) · revaluation surplus → retained earnings direct\n10 Nov: mid-year sale chain on paper, 'got it right' as entries (not typed)\n🟧: 6 Nov 'Cr Building' for a machine · gain-where card unpassed",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 2880,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 196,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n24",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**Definition**\nidentifiable · no physical substance · non-monetary\n+ control + future benefits\n⚠ 29 Oct: got no physical substance + benefits, missed IDENTIFIABLE + NON-MONETARY (carded) · reputation off the books ✓ but reason was only 'can't measure' (also not identifiable)\n7 Nov: ⚠ missed NON-MONETARY · ⚠ training = asset (control). I-N-N mnemonic given.\n10 Nov: the three features COLD ✓ (card 50 → box 2) · control ✓",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 3096,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 196,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n26",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "R&D\nresearch → expense · development → capitalise once ALL 6 criteria met\nno reinstating old expenses\n29 Oct: research expense / development capitalise ✓ (reason: can't prove probable benefits) · no reinstatement ✓\n10 Nov: development 800k ✓ · no reinstating ✓ (skipped the 500k number)",
   "x": 1380,
   "y": 3240,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "n27",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Never an asset\ninternal goodwill · brands · mastheads · customer lists\n⚠ 29 Oct: flipped home-built brand (4M ads) as the asset (carded) → fresh Q: bought customer list ✓\n10 Nov: ⚠ built brand: right pick, wrong reason (card 100)",
   "x": 1380,
   "y": 3420,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n25",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**Ways in**\npurchase · business combination · internal · gov grant · exchange\n⚠ 29 Oct: purchase logic ✓ (training out) but SUBTRACTED install 50k → 950k vs 1,050,000 (carded) · business combination: lumped target's customer list into goodwill (carded) → numbers: goodwill 2M ✓ after calling it a 'loss' first · gov grant: said 'expense' (carded: FV + deferred income, or nominal)\n9 Nov: ⚠ gov-grant licence (ghost 56) got the FV Dr side, missed nominal → 2 cards (grant → P&L not RE · nominal = no grant release)",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 3330,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n28",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**After recognition**\ncost or revaluation (needs active market)\n29 Oct: taxi licences (active market) can revalue, unique patent can't ✓",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 3600,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "4"
  },
  {
   "id": "n29",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**Amortisation**\nfinite → amortise · indefinite → no, impairment test yearly\n⚠ 29 Oct: patent ✓ · goodwill 'reassessed at end of life' → it's impairment-tested EVERY YEAR (carded)\n10 Nov: indefinite brand: no amortise ✓, but ⚠ 'revalue' → it's impairment-tested yearly (card 99) · ⚠ patent part-year 300k → 225k (card 101) · licence 30k ✓",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 3780,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n30",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "**Goodwill**\nprice − FV of net assets · not amortised\n⚠ 29 Oct: called the 3M (10M − 7M) a 'gain on sale' (carded) → own example clicked: person bought 20K in 10K clothes = 10K goodwill, on the BUYER's books\n7 Nov: ⚠ put goodwill on the SELLER's books · ⚠ no 'impairment test yearly'.",
   "x": 880,
   "y": 3960,
   "width": 380,
   "height": 150,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n23",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "## Intangibles (TAS 38)\nSession 10 (17 Oct) · concepts only, Crow builds the numbers\n🟧 7 Nov: WEAKEST block (cards 48–52 all ✗). → 10 Nov 17:30 block done: features + R&D now ✓, amortisation still shaky",
