   "id": "n9",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Exchange\nFV given up + cash · s23–24\n⚠ summed every number (200+120+90 = 410k): didn't know carrying amount = cost − acc dep (ghost card)\n⚠ commercial substance: not in deck\n26 Oct: two-transaction frame (sell old at FV, buy new) clicked → #32 loss version ✓ · #31 ✗ before it\n7 Nov: ⚠ card 32 'no gain or loss' AGAIN (cash folded into the gain).",
   "x": 2800,
   "y": 1119,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n10",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Donation\nFV · Cr capital or other income · s25\n⚠ 26 Oct: flipped giver/receiver TWICE (misread). Receiver: Dr asset at FV, fees capitalised (800k + 15k = 815k). Giver: out at CARRYING AMOUNT → donation expense\n7 Nov: land donation direction ✓ · building fees still as a separate Dr (not capitalised) ⚠.\n10 Nov 20:24: ghost 58 ✗ (fees as their own debit; credit side now ✓) · van: ⚠ capitalised fuel (625k → 620k) · insurance = expense ✓ but reason was a label → test is READY vs RUNNING (3 cards)",
   "x": 2800,
   "y": 1309,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 170,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n11",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Self-construction + borrowing costs (TAS 23)\nqualifying asset · capitalisation period · lesser of actual vs avoidable · s26–31\n⚠ 26 Oct: left construction interest out (500k vs 540k); thought capitalisation runs past READY (it stops; post-ready interest = expense). Depreciation starts when ready ✓\n4 Nov 🟨 real 2021 mid2 P1 (20 pts) walked step by step: WAAE 8,700,000 (slipped 8/12 for 31 Mar → 9/12) · ⚠ read '5%' as over the loan's life (it's per YEAR) · general rate 435,000 / 8,250,000 = 5.27% ✓ · ⚠ applied it to 8.25M borrowed instead of the 5.7M WAAE left over · capitalise lesser: 510,390 vs actual 645,000. ⚠ senior's annotated answer (5.7% blended) is WRONG. NEXT: redo P1 from a blank page on paper.\n7 Nov: P1 redo ~8–10/20 (guess): WAAE ✓ · interest 435k ✓ · ⚠ general/specific pick · ⚠ denominator · ⚠ general part 434,775 AGAIN (rate on the LOANS, not the leftover WAAE) · ⚠ said 'capitalise the higher'. Variant (actual < avoidable → capitalise actual 760k, expense 0) ✓ after a re-teach. NEXT: P1 cold.\n10 Nov: clean Q ✓ (WAAE 5M, 9.5%: general 285k + specific 200k = 485k; the 'rate × loans' miss didn't recur) · ceiling variant ✗ 190k (card 96) → rebuilt in pieces: ⚠ general base typed 240k (paper 260k, card 73) · ⚠ 'why subtract' right pick, wrong reason (card 97) · WAAE ✓ · weighted rate 7% ✓ · ceiling 350k ✓ · full solo: general 160k ✓ but ⚠ handed 160k in as the TOTAL (250k, card 98)\n10 Nov 18:46: REAL 2021 mid2 P1 cold on paper → key 510,390, he says 'perfect' (not typed: cards Thu–Fri are the real check). The POINTS on that paper sit here + in the reval/impairment chains.",
   "x": 2800,
   "y": 1479,
   "width": 360,
   "height": 222,
   "color": "2"
  },
  {
   "id": "n12",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Dismantling cost (ARO)\nPV into cost, unwind as interest · s36–41\n26 Oct (GPT): covered, strong on the entries · recheck: PV = time value, not certainty",
