  },
  {
   "id": "n7",
   "type": "text",
   "text": "Deferred payment\ncash price; the rest is interest · s20–21\n⚠ read 'instalments' (paying in parts) as 'installation'; under that reading 280,000 was logical. Concept itself: cost = CASH price, the extra = interest (ghost card)\nsolid: 1 Jan entry · ⚠ 30 June interest: used 250k × full year and 'interest payable'; it's 200k × 10% × 6/12 = 10,000 interest EXPENSE (ghost card)\n10 Nov 🟩: both cards (cost = cash price · 30 June entry) passed cold",
   "x": 2800,
